p = "docs/LEDGER.md"
s = open(p, encoding="utf-8", newline="").read()
nl = "\r\n" if "\r\n" in s else "\n"
anchor = "- **E4a DECISIONS ON A POSSIBLY DEGENERATE GROUP RESIDUAL"
assert s.count(anchor) == 1 and "(A) BUILT, THE WALK MEMO" not in s
new = ("- **(A) BUILT, THE WALK MEMO (2026-10-20; the reviewer 21:18, 21:28): TETHER_WALK_MEMO (default ON), TETHER_WALK_MEMO_CHECK (default OFF, a check-run switch).** "
       "THE SITE (the S2c box, sp80 8 cycles, 155 s): the index walk (_index_reach, 47.8 s over 245 walks, 1.83M _compiled calls at about 20 us) is the recognition cost; _index_for's whole-walk store (_reach_index) is keyed with frozenset(changed), which the walk never reads (it reaches it only through lit / cands / others, already in the key), so it missed almost every step; a second caller, _no_search_want (from _derived_wants and _g1_wants), walked with no memo. "
       "THE READ: a walk reads its arguments, the atoms' token and compile signature, the compile cache and, in _compiled, the held index -- _INDEX_STORE[(sig, entry, role)], set once from lib.view and the atoms, never cleared or rewritten (one write site), the route's library fixed for the process (_lib_view's own docstring) -- so within a process the held index is a pure function of (signature, entry, role) and the key's signature covers it (the reviewer's (b), by proof); _derived_now() feeds only an _INDEX_N counter, not the result. A walk WRITES _spent, the late-tier counters, the 7l kind landings (this step's dk) and the asked tally (_ak_asked, read only by write_ak). "
       "THE BUILD: _index_reach keeps each lit entry's walk under (the library's id, atoms token, signature, entry, slot, mine, partner, others, targets); _walk_one walks one entry into its own record (views and causes in walk order with their first entry and counts, refusals, _spent charges, landings, held-role asks) and _walk_apply merges a record into the walk exactly as the walk would, charges its _spent (the reviewer's (a): the budget is a decision cap, so a hit spends what a walk would), lands its kinds under this step's dk and, on a hit, replays its asks. The asked tally has ONE writer, _ak_note, called by _compiled at its two sites and by the replay. A walk stops only between late entries, so every kept entry is whole. _index_for's whole-walk store retires under the arm (one memo for one quantity); it is cleared at retarget with the other board memos; the memo_sizes row carries its size under the arm. "
       "test_walk_memo (gridworld_arc_s1, 15 steps, ON / CHECK / OFF): ON 212,793 entry hits, 33,680 misses; (1) the CHECK run's 212,793 kept walks each equal their fresh walk (views, causes, refusals, charges, landings, asks), 0 disagree, and ON's 2,714 rows are the CHECK run's (books' walk_memo_* counters, the arms lists and wall_s masked) -- no decision moves; (2) a planted compile signature: the next step 0 hits, 14,812 misses; OFF moves no counter." + nl)
s = s.replace(anchor, new + anchor)
open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="").write(s)
print("ok")
